# Test fixtures must stay byte-exact across platforms: the WAV/PPM loaders and the
# RMS thresholds in the Phase 10 harness depend on the exact bytes, so never apply
# line-ending conversion to them (CI checks out on Linux).
*.wav binary
*.ppm binary

# Shell scripts must stay LF: CI (and the fetch/setup scripts) run on Linux, where
# a CRLF shebang line breaks the interpreter. Normalize regardless of a
# contributor's core.autocrlf.
*.sh text eol=lf
